# `FLOWCHART-ROLE-KEYWORDS` / `UNSAFE-DEFAULT-ELIMINATION` §3: a bare `node` under `flowchart` is ROLE-UNSTATED. It does NOT
# default to `process` — a flowchart node may be a datastore, an annotation or
# a state, so a default here could assert a falsehood that no inspection of the
# figure would catch. The model therefore OMITS `role` on `store` and `hint`,
# and a reading agent can tell "the author said nothing" from "the author said
# process" — which is the distinction the whole vocabulary buys.
figdown 0.2 flowchart
process step "Write the record"
node    store "Journal" shape=cylinder
node    hint
flow down
flowline step -> store
flowline store -> hint
